      "claim": "Observational studies that compare athletes or highly active students with non‑athletes typically find only a modest positive correlation with academic outcomes.",
      "evidence": "Meta‑analysis of 70 studies (Singh et al., 2022) reports an average effect size of d = 0.12 (small) for the relationship between regular physical activity and GPA; studies focusing on elite mastery show similar or smaller effects.",
